3. **`shouldSpillUserMessage`**: `utf8.encode(text).length` — encodes the whole (potentially multi-MB) text just to count bytes. For a 10MB message this is fine-ish (one allocation), but it happens on EVERY user message — including small ones. `utf8.encode` on every message is a small cost. Acceptable, but for very large messages (say 50MB), encoding is wasteful yet still done once. Performance note: could approximate with `text.length` for the floor check first (chars >= bytes), i.e. if `text.length <= userThreshold` skip. Minor suggestion.

